  "source": {
    "title": "Armagh Guardian, 20 January 1905, p. 5 (\"Armagh municipal election: a Nationalist majority largely reduced\"; \"Declaration of the poll\")",
    "publisher": "Armagh Guardian (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every name and figure read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council. The Unionists agreed not to contest the South Ward if the Nationalists withdrew their two candidates from the East Ward, so only the North Ward went to a poll (Monday 16 January 1905; the Irish News, 18 January 1905, p. 5, reports the North Ward, which it calls St. Patrick's Ward, as polled \"yesterday\"). The poll closed at 8 o'clock and about 11 the returning officer declared all six Nationalists elected. The paper prints surnames only. Majority of the highest Nationalist over the highest Unionist, 22."
}
